.SS "int32_t schultz_events_set_pointer_source (\fBschultz_events\fP * events, uint32_t source)"

.PP
Says what is driving the pointer from here on\&. The platform layer sets this as it translates each event, before handing it to the router, and every event the router sends afterwards carries it\&. It stays as set until it is changed, because a run of events from one finger all come from the same source\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIevents\fP The routing state\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIsource\fP SCHULTZ_POINTER_MOUSE or SCHULTZ_POINTER_TOUCH\&. 
