.SS "int32_t schultz_events_set_delete_by_codepoint (\fBschultz_events\fP * events, int32_t on)"

.PP
Says that a delete key removes one codepoint rather than a whole character\&. For a platform that has no keys to report and works out what changed instead, sending one backspace for every codepoint it removed\&. See \fCone_codepoint\fP on \fBschultz_event\fP for what goes wrong without this\&.
.PP
A host that reports real key presses never calls this\&. One that translates them from a platform text field sets it while that is where the keys are coming from, and clears it if a real keyboard is attached\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIevents\fP The event system\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fIon\fP Nonzero to mark delete keys from here on\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, or SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int32_t schultz_events_perform (\fBschultz_events\fP * events, \fBschultz_handle\fP node, uint32_t action)"

.PP
Carries out one of a node's declared actions\&. The way something other than a hand asks a widget to act\&. An assistive technology telling a screen reader user's button to press arrives here, and is turned into the same event a real press produces, so that what a screen reader can do and what a mouse can do cannot drift apart\&.
.PP
The action is refused unless the node declares it in its accessibility schema, which is what stops a caller reaching past what a widget offers\&.
.PP
Increment and decrement are delivered as a right or left arrow key, because that is the input a range widget already understands\&. A widget that answers neither will not move\&.
.PP
SCHULTZ_ACTION_SET_VALUE is not handled here: a value needs a payload, and this call carries none\&. SCHULTZ_ACTION_SCROLL is not either, because bringing a node into view belongs to the scroll view that holds it; see schultz_scroll_view_reveal\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIevents\fP The routing state\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.br
\fInode\fP The node to act on\&. Must name a live node\&. 
.br
\fIaction\fP One of the SCHULTZ_ACTION_* values, exactly one\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT when the action is not one this handles or the node does not declare it, or SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_HANDLE\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBschultz_handle\fP schultz_events_captured (const \fBschultz_events\fP * events)"

.PP
Returns the node holding the pointer capture\&. Set on press and cleared on release\&. While it is set, motion is delivered to it as a drag no matter where the pointer goes\&.
